Ok. I have developed an application, that given an openEHR AQL must:

1) find affected templates
2) normalize the AQL query to:

1) decompose it with different OR clauses if necessary when is affecting different templates.
2) substitute the paths per absolute paths in the query.

You have to take into account the FROM/CONTAINS block and getting tha max hierarchy in the openehr RM. Then scan all the webtemplates to find those templates affected by the AQL , get the aqlpaths from the web templates and substitute the corresponding aliases while probably building a full hierarchical CONTAINS block from composition to the smallest component necessary in that query.

original query

SELECT 
  a/time/value as AdministrationTime,
  im_item/value as ImmunizationItem
FROM EHR e
CONTAINS (
  ACTION a[Immunization managemeenEHR-EHR-ACTION.medication.v1]
  AND DV_CODED_TEXT im_item[at0020, 'Immunization item']
)

normalized

SELECT 
  c/uid/value as CompositionID,
  c/content[openEHR-EHR-SECTION.immunisation_list.v0]/items[openEHR-EHR-ACTION.medication.v1]/time/value as AdministrationTime,
  c/content[openEHR-EHR-SECTION.immunisation_list.v0]/items[openEHR-EHR-ACTION.medication.v1]/description[at0017]/items[at0020]/value as ImmunizationItem
FROM EHR e
CONTAINS COMPOSITION c[openEHR-EHR-COMPOSITION.vaccination_list.v0]


SELECT 
  c/uid/value as CompositionID,
  c/content[openEHR-EHR-SECTION.immunisation_list.v0]/items[openEHR-EHR-ACTION.medication.v1]/time/value as AdministrationTime,
  c/content[openEHR-EHR-SECTION.immunisation_list.v0]/items[openEHR-EHR-ACTION.medication.v1]/description[at0017]/items[at0020]/value as ImmunizationItem
FROM EHR e
CONTAINS (COMPOSITION c[openEHR-EHR-COMPOSITION.vaccination_list.v1] OR COMPOSITION c[openEHR-EHR-COMPOSITION.vaccination_list.v2])



SELECT 
  c/uid/value as CompositionID,
  c/content[openEHR-EHR-SECTION.immunisation_list.v0]/items[openEHR-EHR-ACTION.medication.v1]/time/value OR c/content[openEHR-EHR-SECTION.immunisation_list.v2]/items[openEHR-EHR-ACTION.medication.v1]/time/value as AdministrationTime 
  c/content[openEHR-EHR-SECTION.immunisation_list.v0]/items[openEHR-EHR-ACTION.medication.v1]/description[at0017]/items[at0020]/value as ImmunizationItem
FROM EHR e
CONTAINS COMPOSITION c[openEHR-EHR-COMPOSITION.vaccination_list.v0]





SELECT 
  a/time/value as AdministrationTime,
  im_item/value as ImmunizationItem
FROM EHR e
CONTAINS (
  ACTION a[openEHR-EHR-ACTION.medication.v1, 'Immunization management']
  AND DV_CODED_TEXT im_item[at0020, 'Immunization item']
)

SELECT 
  a/time/value as AdministrationTime,
  b/value as BatchID
FROM EHR e
CONTAINS (
  ACTION a[openEHR-EHR-ACTION.medication.v1, 'Immunization management']
  AND CLUSTER med[openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER.medication.v2, 'Medication details']
  AND ELEMENT b[at0150, 'Batch ID']
)


SELECT 
  a/time/value as AdministrationTime,
  cd/items[at0132]/value as ConstituentName
FROM EHR e
CONTAINS (
  ACTION a[openEHR-EHR-ACTION.medication.v1, 'Immunization management']
  AND CLUSTER med[openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER.medication.v2, 'Medication details']
  AND CLUSTER cd[openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER.medication.v2, 'Constituent details']
)


SELECT 
  a/time/value as AdministrationTime,
  COALESCE(im_item/value, b/value) as ImmunizationDetail
FROM EHR e
CONTAINS (
  ACTION a[openEHR-EHR-ACTION.medication.v1, 'Immunization management']
  AND (DV_CODED_TEXT im_item[at0020, 'Immunization item'] OR ELEMENT b[at0150, 'Batch ID'])
)


SELECT 
  ad/items[at0002]/value as DocumentCreationDate
FROM EHR e
CONTAINS (
  EVENT_CONTEXT ec
  AND CLUSTER ad[openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER.admin_salut.v0]
)





1.a) Queries that we know the ehr_id

one unique composition collection
filter though ehr_id with $match
often depending on the contains clauses we will need to filter though nodes field
transverse the full where clauses with elemmatch on normal composition


1.b) Queries that we know the ehr_id

two compositions, one with original compositions, and another with the metaIndex info,
filter though ehr_id and often depending on the contains clauses we will need to filter though nodes field using $search
match for the rest of the conditions afer a lookup
transverse the full where clauses with elemmatch on normal composition

2) Population level queries

two compositions, one with original compositions, and another with the metaIndex info,
we would need to add attributes in the nodes field and corresponding index

filter though ehr_id and often depending on the contains clauses we will need to filter though nodes field using $search
match for the rest of the conditions afer a lookup
transverse the full where clauses with elemmatch on normal composition

*****************************
1. Use Atlas Search nodes for isolating $search
2. Rest of the pipeline could be managed by dedicated Analytics nodes (stalliness of min 90s)



